@startuml
' Behavior 3: recovery and reconciliation after a failure.
' Authored in Slice 2. Renders through scripts/render-diagrams.sh.
' Store-local inventory and the master record are both projections of the per-source
' event log. A hot standby of the master takes over at once; a copy that lost state
' rebuilds and then replays from the authoritative log. When the events a store would
' replay are no longer in its Outbox it sends a snapshot instead, and the master replaces
' that store's figures.
!include style.puml
title Components-and-Connectors view: behavior, recovery and reconciliation

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 235

participant "Store Agent" as SA #93C47D
database "Store durable log\n(Outbox + local\nevent log)" as SLOG #8E7CC3
database "Store-Local\nInventory" as SLI #8E7CC3
participant "Communications\nFront-End" as CFE #F1C232
database "CFE event store" as CFEDB #8E7CC3
participant "Central Master\nInventory" as CMI #F1C232
participant "Standby Master\nInventory" as SMI #F1C232

== Master failure: the standby takes over (AV-3) ==
CMI -> CMI : process or host fails
note over CMI : a master that cannot renew its\nlease stops serving queries, so only\none master answers at a time
note over SMI : a second subscription that has applied\nevery event, so it is already current;\nmissed heartbeats detect the failure
SMI -> SMI : takes over the Inventory Query only after\nthe active master's lease has expired;\nquery clients fail over within seconds
note over CFE, CFEDB : the CFE keeps accepting events and\ndelivering them to the standby; stores\nkeep publishing
CMI -> SMI : on restart, copies the standby's state\nand per-source applied positions
CMI -> CFE : subscribe (resume), then resync
CMI -> CFE : replay from the copied positions
CFE -> CFEDB : read retained events (replay read path)
CFE --> CMI : missing events in source order
note over CMI : applies idempotently, then\nrejoins as the standby

== Store reconnect or restart (AV-1, TEST-2) ==
SA -> SLOG : after a restart: replay\nthe local event log
SLOG --> SA : events in source order
SA -> SLI : rebuild projection (idempotent)
SA -> CFE : resync (per-source sequence watermarks)\nIEP / TLS 1.3 mutual certs [secure]
alt history complete (the normal path, any outage length)
  SA -> CFE : replay unacknowledged Outbox events
  note over SA, CFE : backlog drains at up to 2,000 events/s per store\nwhile live sales continue (PERF-4)
else events to replay no longer in the Outbox
  CFE --> SA : snapshot required
  SA -> CFE : Store Snapshot (stock per product,\nsequence position)
  CFE -> CMI : deliver Store Snapshot (also to the standby)
  note over CMI : replaces that store's figures and\ncontinues from the snapshot's sequence\nposition (state resynchronization)
end

legend right
  Both inventory copies are projections of the per-source
  event log. Only the master holding the lease serves queries.
  A failed master copy copies the standby's state and per-source
  applied positions, then replays from those positions in the
  CFE event store. A store replays its Outbox after an outage
  of any length.
  Replay is idempotent, so no event is lost or applied twice.
  A store whose events are no longer in its Outbox sends a
  snapshot, and the master continues from its position.
endlegend
@enduml
